{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying","id":725511,"title":"Solar War is terrifying","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-25T03:55:58-07:00","id":725511,"title":"Solar War is terrifying","content":"Just like in previous editions Tiger Warrior Training Technique makes its return. This time it doesn't fiddle with individual stats but rather it allows you to to turn any group of soldiers into Elite troops with Elite Drill in a month. Further the Solar can grant their elite troops +2 might against CoD's and Giants as well as perfect morale which means they can never fail rout checks unless magic is involved.<br /> <br /> <b>How powerful are these troops?</b><br /> <br /> Before any other mechanics come into play, default Elite troops have 11 dice to attack, 12 damage, 10 soak and 7 health levels. Their default defence is Evasion 3, Parry 5.<br /> Size: +1 Attack/Damage/Soak/HL per point of size.<br /> Elite Drill: +2 Defense and +2 to command rolls.<br /> Might 2: +2 Attack/Damage and +1 Defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> This leaves them as Attack 15, Damage 17, Soak 15, Magnitude(Health) 12, Evasion 5, Parry 7 against most enemies and Attack 17, Damage 19, Defense 6/8 against Giants or Creatures of darkness.<br /> <br /> We can compare that to a Tyrant Lizard, which has Attack 11-13, Damage 12-16, Defense 4/6 and Soak 15.<br /> <br /> <b>You've only used one charm so far, what about the rest of the War tree?</b><br /> <br /> The very first charm in Solar War, War God Descendent, let's you increase size by 1 during Join Battle, as you can see that's pretty good. Now in addition to various charms that involve rallying (Healing) and stratagems (Scene-long buffs you get by out-rolling the other general before the battle starts), Solar War gives quite a few bonuses to Order Actions, specifically Double 8's (Ideal Battle Knowledge Prana), reroll 6's (Four Glories Meditation) and almost most notably, the Solar War Excellency.<br /> <br /> <b>What is an order action?</b><br /> <br /> The Order action is a combat action (That can't be flurried) where a commander or hero in an army rolls ([Charisma, Appearance, or Intelligence]+ War) against difficulty 1. All successes on that roll will be applied to all actions the battle-group takes that turn.<br /> <br /> All things considered a Solar General using 21 dice and the relevant charms should probably get about 17.5 successes which brings the Battlegroups Attack to 32-33, enough to reliably hit any reasonably achievable defence with plenty to spare. These dice will apply to all rolls for the entire turn including Rush and Disengage rolls.<br /> <br /> Additionally Battlegroups can use a specialized form of grapple called Engage with the same die-pool they use for their normal attacks with the limitation of being unable to use the Restrain/Drag or Throw moves.<br /> <br /> <b>What about Stratagems?</b><br /> <br /> There's not a lot of example stratagems in the book, the most notable ones for these purposes are the Ambush (All attacks in the first round are ambush, the next 3 rounds are surprise) and Pincer (All enemies suffer -1 onslaught throughout the entire battle). Through the use of General of the All-Seeing Sun a Solar general can activate up to (essence) stratagems at once. They can also use Battle Path Ascendant and Transcendent Warlord's Genius to roll Join Battle and create a new stratagem whenever they empty an enemy magnitude track, although I fail to wrap my head around how that works.<br /> <br /> <b>What's the fastest way to break the battle-group system with a home-brewed effect?</b><br /> <br /> Any effect which allow you to flurry or use order actions reflexively would make the character possessing it roll over everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-25-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:02:54-07:00","id":725544,"title":"","content":"Seems like its working as intended. So he will make men out of them, mysterious as the dark side of the moon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:05:17-07:00","id":725546,"title":"","content":"Holy...wow never fail route checks? Double freaking EIGHTS on order actions? God damn, that's horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:15:42-07:00","id":725552,"title":"","content":"Battle-Visionary's Foresight lets the player pick two Stratagems and set them face-down. If their foe picks one of those two Stratagems, the player reveal it and basically go &quot;YOU ACTIVATED MY TRAP STRATAGEM!&quot; and counter the stratagem perfectly.<br /> <br /> This is GLORIOUS","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:21:47-07:00","id":725556,"title":"","content":"My only issue is that Tiger Warrior Technique only trains one kind of soldier, bad ass heavy infantry. If I want light cavalry, or Brides of Ahlat, or mounted archers, or guerilla warriors I'm pretty much SOL. Even worse if I want to train a battle group of summoned Blood Apes.<br /> <br /> But yeah War is super scary, even scarier when you battle group something with charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:30:14-07:00","id":725560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying?p=725556#post725556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only issue is that Tiger Warrior Technique only trains one kind of soldier, bad ass heavy infantry. If I want light cavalry, or Brides of Ahlat, or mounted archers, or guerilla warriors I'm pretty much SOL. Even worse if I want to train a battle group of summoned Blood Apes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just a matter of switching the equipment? The default elite troops use Medium Weapons and Heavy Armor. However I believe the battlegroup rules do rather favor heavy troops over light troops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T05:21:21-07:00","id":725593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying?p=725560#post725560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that just a matter of switching the equipment? The default elite troops use Medium Weapons and Heavy Armor. However I believe the battlegroup rules do rather favor heavy troops over light troops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elite troops are elite troops. What gear you give them is up to you. The will all get the bonuses. At least I don't see anywhere why you couldn't apply it to blood apes or brides of Ahlat or the Yellow Cavalry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T05:26:08-07:00","id":725607,"title":"","content":"I can't decide if I like Solar War or Solar Sail better, but both are gonna see use in my seafaring game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:11:42-07:00","id":726224,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I always read &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">An order action both determines what the targeted battle group will do on its next turn and adds its successes to the battle group\u2019s dice pools for all actions taken during that turn</span></span>&quot; as indicating that the successes rolled are applied as bonus dice to the subsequent pool, which is still really good, but not quite as good as you're describing, Zironic. I certainly could be wrong, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:31:29-07:00","id":726304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying?p=726224#post726224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I always read &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">An order action both determines what the targeted battle group will do on its next turn and adds its successes to the battle group\u2019s dice pools for all actions taken during that turn</span></span>&quot; as indicating that the successes rolled are applied as bonus dice to the subsequent pool, which is still really good, but not quite as good as you're describing, Zironic. I certainly could be wrong, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, you're probably correct. What makes the Order command particularly scary is that it lasts for the entire turn, so that means that any rush or disengage rolls the battlegroup gets involved with will be huge. Also worth noting is that Battlegroups have access to a special grapple attack called 'Engage' which they get to use with their full attack pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:41:53-07:00","id":726312,"title":"","content":"I hadn't considered the reactive benefits of an Order. Yeah, consistent orders make them much harder to escape. Even if the Solar themself is unavailable for such orders, having a trusted lieutenant onhand to take over command is worth doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T10:43:26-07:00","id":726481,"title":"","content":"Orders, man. So nasty.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying#post725511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All things considered a Solar General using 21 dice and the relevant charms should probably get about 15 successes after which the battle group will probably average 7 successes of their own. Against a reasonably high defense such as 8, that leaves them with 14 threshhold successes for raw damage of 31 which is applied to all characters in contact with the battlegroup and rolls into normal damage once it's drained all initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>23 dice - maxed stats/Excellency and a basic Stunt. With Reroll 6s and Double 8s, that gives you almost exactly 17.5 average successes - so, 16 or 17 threshold successes. Tiger Warriors, then, can be throwing over 30 dice reliably. That should hit basically any Defense number in the game.<br /> <br /> Is this too much? Do Orders need a dice cap? Maybe. As with the Tyrant Lizard abuse people talk about, this army can also be unwieldy in many situations (say, fighting against a sorcerer in a small room atop their tall tower), doesn't get the kind of easy fast travel groups can, and opens itself up to loads of plot hooks involving famine, plague, dissension in the ranks, and so on. That probably means it <i>should</i> win an all-out fight where it gets to do its thing against another Solar who invested the same XP in being the ultimate solo combatant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T10:59:27-07:00","id":726496,"title":"","content":"Yes. The overwhelming power of a Size 5 Battlegroup lead by a Solar is completely appropriate just because of the context where you can actually use a Size 5 Battlegroup. What they're absolutely best at is murdering large monsters or other armies, thanks to being granted contextual might by TWTT they're actually more or less exactly as powerful as an army of the same size containing only Elite Drilled Blood Apes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-25-2015, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:09:54-07:00","id":726541,"title":"","content":"... how in Octavian's name would you ever impart Elite Drill on <i>Blood Apes</i>?<br /> <br /> Cloud Arsenals, maybe. Some sort of hive mind insect demon, sure. But Blood Apes? The mind boggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:14:08-07:00","id":726552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying?p=726541#post726541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... how in Octavian's name would you ever impart Elite Drill on <i>Blood Apes</i>?<br /> <br /> Cloud Arsenals, maybe. Some sort of hive mind insect demon, sure. But Blood Apes? The mind boggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why you had all the Solars assassinated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:33:37-07:00","id":726584,"title":"","content":"So far as I can tell, the way to try and deal with Battle Groups is essentially to deal as much damage as you possibly can to them before they attack. Reduce their Size and thus their bonuses. But yeah, led by a Solar general? That's going to be a nightmare. Of course, if you manage to take out the General, then the Battle Group is a lot easier to deal with, and of course the General needs to be giving those orders and thus cannot attack. Still, terrifyingly effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:49:51-07:00","id":726637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/725511-solar-war-is-terrifying?p=726496#post726496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The overwhelming power of a Size 5 Battlegroup lead by a Solar is completely appropriate just because of the context where you can actually use a Size 5 Battlegroup. What they're absolutely best at is murdering large monsters or other armies, thanks to being granted contextual might by TWTT they're actually more or less exactly as powerful as an army of the same size containing only Elite Drilled Blood Apes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to agree with this, a lot.<br /> <br /> So, it's been said by the Dev team that they wanted the mechanics to model the setting. In previous editions, there was genuinely little reason for, say, an experienced Dawn Caste to raise an army if he wants to go trash a place - armies kind of sucked and weren't worth the trouble when you could just hoist your grand killstick and lay waste to them in short order, personally, at little or no risk to yourself.<br /> <br /> This was bad for the setting and bad for the game, because raising a grand army and marching on your enemies is not only <i>awesome</i>, it's what you really should <i>want to do</i> because it's the most effective (maybe <i>only </i>effective) way to accomplish your stated goal, when your stated goal is something like &quot;conquer a city&quot; or &quot;fight another army.&quot; You can't do this all the time, however - armies take up lots of space, move slowly, require lots of logistical support and cannot be easily leveraged against discrete individuals or targets. They exist at the army scale, and only really work against other things that exist on that scale. But they should be the clear weapon of choice when you are operating on that scale.<br /> <br /> Now consider the 3E model. If you hear that a full-blown Wyld Hunt marshaling a House Legion of imperial soldiers is bearing down on you, you should A) be rightly worried about the danger that force represents, and B) want to answer with an army of your own. Within this context, that is what you need to do. Striding out and dealing with it personally might be possible, but even a Solar should only do that if he's foolish or desperate, because the odds are stacked heavily against him. <i>That's how Solars die.</i> A better idea would be to leave the area, either abandoning your plans there (essentially a defeat) or evading the army until you can build a force that can challenge it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, an experienced Solar with War Charms including TWTT, resources to equip and field an army, and weeks to prepare will be and <i>should </i>be an absolute nightmare on the battlefield. It's what the entire Dawn Caste was made for in the first place, after all. You <i>do not</i> just roll up on Hannibal and his armies on open ground and expect to win, because in this context Hannibal is <i>king shit</i>. That's what Solar generals do. <i>They win</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:05:31-07:00","id":726692,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I suddenly feel reminded of the <i>other</i> angle - Solars specialising in fighting as a small group against a huge army.<br /> More specifically, this Discworld Quote... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Interesting Times</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But: six old men . . . and the Empire had almost a million men under arms. When you looked at the odds in the cold light of dawn, or even this rather pleasant warm light of dawn, they made you stop and do the arithmetic of death. If the Plan went wrong . . . Cohen bit his lip thoughtfully. If the Plan went wrong, it'd take weeks to kill all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}